PURPOSE
-------

This file reconciles recovered study tables, documented numerical results,
derived calculations, manuscript-facing figures, and computational artifacts
against the current computational source-of-truth.

The purpose is to determine:

1. which tables and figures are supported by documented study records;
2. which numerical values are directly traceable to recovered records;
3. which values are mathematically derived from documented values;
4. which outputs require recovery or recreation of the executed COMSOL model;
5. which tables/figures may currently be used only as provisional or
   documentation-level artifacts;
6. which tables/figures must remain withheld from final manuscript claims
   until computational execution evidence is recovered.

IMPORTANT EVIDENCE PRINCIPLE
-----------------------------

A table or figure may be numerically internally consistent without being
independently verified as a COMSOL execution output.

The following distinctions must therefore be maintained:

A. MODEL SPECIFICATION
   Describes what the computational model was intended or documented to do.

B. DOCUMENTED STUDY VALUE
   A value appearing in recovered study notes, tables, scripts, or records.

C. DERIVED VALUE
   A value mathematically calculated from documented values.

D. RECOVERED EXECUTION ARTIFACT
   A machine-readable or native computational output directly produced by
   the executed model.

E. VERIFIED EXECUTION EVIDENCE
   A recovered artifact that is traceable to the executed model and can be
   independently audited.

Only categories D and E can establish final computational execution status.

